ollback-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 10288, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01X2U9B5YvqVRKVrTSHVscuh", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 11677, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It's healthy again, and the error rate dropped from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\nv2.3.0 was the most recent release that had been healthy in production. v2.3.1 is the unhealthy release, and v2.3.1-rc was only healthy in staging, so I didn't use either.\n\nI opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the rollback and the reason for it, and it paged the on-call engineer. The next step is to investigate the v2.3.1 failure before anyone re-releases it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01MBf1fsmzaQqwa2EW3yAoAi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Bd48nK9v89yq6iZaWEfvHT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is the unhealthy one, and v2.3.1-rc was only healthy in staging. I'll roll back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Y8eCFVE8g9LZCs8DA9hLFA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Vx7nmgdxqbmWcJuPxd92bE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01X2U9B5YvqVRKVrTSHVscuh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18). I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy and was not redeployed. v2.3.1-rc was healthy only in staging and was not used. Next steps: confirm error rate recovery, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any re-release.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It's healthy again, and the error rate dropped from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\nv2.3.0 was the most recent release that had been healthy in production. v2.3.1 is the unhealthy release, and v2.3.1-rc was only healthy in staging, so I didn't use either.\n\nI opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the rollback and the reason for it, and it paged the on-call engineer. The next step is to investigate the v2.3.1 failure before anyone re-releases it.", "type": "text"}]}]}